WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.740
It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.640
Today, I'm going to be answering questions about love and romance

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.480
because,

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.080
you know,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.260
I'm such an expert in the field.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.580
[Intro music]

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.760
"Why am I so scared of rejection?"

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.120
Well, cause it's scary.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.700
But the important thing to remember is that

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:21.960
EVERYONE is afraid of rejection,

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.200
they just don't seem that way because you're not busy living inside of THEIR thoughts.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.920
"How do I know if my boyfriend is about to porpoise?"

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.660
Okay, the first sign I would look for

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.760
is that your boyfriend might be spending a lot of time in the water.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.940
In fact, if your boyfriend is about to porpoise,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.540
he might feel increasingly uncomfortable on land.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.480
He may also start to look increasingly less human and more dolphin shaped,

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.740
but without the beak.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.200
So yeah I would say if you notice any of that stuff,

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.280
then your boyfriend is probably going to porpoise pretty soon.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.060
Oh wait.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.060
You probably meant,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.780
"how can I tell when my boyfriend's gonna PROpose?"

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:54.780
Mmm.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.940
See why spelling matters.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.940
The number one way to find out if your boyfriend is going to propose

00:00:58.940 --> 00:00:59.980
is to ask him

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.340
and to talk about it

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.760
because it's weird that in our culture, for some reason,

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.960
marriage is something thrust upon women.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.740
Like boys get to spend six months deciding if they want to get married,

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.760
but then the girl only has like ten seconds to say yes or no.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.800
"Where are all the nerdy girls?"

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.780
Okay, dude, I don't want you to freak out,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:16.400
but

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.260
they're right here.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.940
Seriously dude, they're like watching us right now.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.020
So yeah, just keep cool,

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.240
don't let them know that you know that they're here

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.080
and just, you know, play it confident.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.820
"Is it weird having your first kiss?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.520
I want to know because I think I might have my first kiss soon, and I don't want to be too nervous."

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.400
Okay, first,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.420
I need to know if you mean like,

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:32.920
[mwah, mwah]

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:33.420
kiss,

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:33.960
or if you mean like

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.750
[bwok, bwok, bwok]

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:35.480
kiss.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.540
By the way, that was not intended as a demonstration of proper kissing technique.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.500
Because like the

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.160
[mwah, mwah] kiss,

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.260
no big whoop, nothing to be nervous about.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.060
Though like [bla-la-la-la] kiss,

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.220
I'm gonna level with you,

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.740
you should be nervous about that.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.660
Listen, it's probably gonna go poorly,

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.060
but if I can give you just one piece of advice:

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.500
the human tongue is a fantastic organ,

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.820
it's great for tasting,

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.300
without it, speech would be impossible,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.560
but I would argue that it should not be the primary combatant of any kiss.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.560
You know how the Marines always say that they're first to fight?

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.940
The tongue should not be first to kiss.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.020
The tongue is like the Navy Seals.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.460
You know, they're like in and out so fast,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.300
you'll almost didn't even know they were there.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.500
"What is the average number of times boys need to be broken up with

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.780
before they realize that girls don't like needy clingy boys?"

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.380
53.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.420
"When two nerdfighters are in nerdfighter like, but then they need some time apart,

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.140
what is that phenomenon called?"

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.340
Breaking up.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.720
"Is it still acceptable to ask someone out by writing them a note

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.000
in which you ask them to check either yes, or no?"

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.920
Do you think it's still allowed to write a note where you ask someone to check yes or no?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.200
[Sarah]: It was never a good thing.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.280
It totally worked with Jennifer Keene in third grade,

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:39.874
so back off.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.100
[Sarah]: Um.. It works!

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.560
[Sarah]: I'm just saying that it's not, it's never been cool.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.820
[Sarah]: It's always the whimp's way.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.540
What do you recommend instead?

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.860
[Sarah]: Ask them.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:51.740
With your voice?

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:52.480
[Sarah]: Yeah.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.460
What if it quivers?

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.620
"How does a nerd win over a beauty queen?"

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.480
I don't know,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.860
maybe I'd start by offering it peanut butter flavored treats.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:00.640
No, wait,

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.000
that's how you win over a puppy.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.740
I don't know how to win over a beauty queen,

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.600
I've never tried.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.680
"I'm almost 18 and I've never been out on a date or had a boyfriend

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.400
and then I get really shy around guys,

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.740
is that weird or not weird?"

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.840
It's not weird

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.520
and you might be surprised to learn HOW not weird it is.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.940
But, as far as getting shy around guys goes,

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.340
it's important to remember that they are, you know,

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.340
people

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.100
in exactly the same way that girls are people.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:27.640
"Is it still called nerdfighter like if one person in the relationship is a nerdfighter and the other isn't?"

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.300
No.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:28.920
That's called

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:29.900
"internerdial dating."

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.680
"Do guys really not like girls who are smarter than them?"

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:35.640
The venn diagram of guys who don't like smart girls

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.820
and guys you don't want to date

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.820
is a circle.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.460
"Is breaking up over text message bad?"

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.200
Yes.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.420
"How do you get over crushing shyness to ask a boy out on a date?"

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.140
Just ask.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.120
I mean, actually, call him right now,

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.860
before you even finish watching this video.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:50.960
Just call him

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:51.660
and say,

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.500
"John Green said I had to call you.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.720
I like you a little bit

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.820
I want to go out on a date.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:56.600
No big whoop."

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.900
Hank, thanks for being awesome,

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.340
and I'll see you tomorrow.

